    {
      "id": "d6b140f9-f137-4045-8700-9325d0ee4624",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Log wallet transfers to Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\nThe Qersh app on the merchant's phone posts every incoming wallet transfer (Vodafone Cash, Orange Cash, e& money, InstaPay) to the Webhook node as a signed JSON delivery. The Code node checks the signature on the raw body with the connection key and refuses anything else with 401. A valid delivery is answered with 200 at once, the connection test is left alone, and each transfer becomes one row in your sheet: time, amount, payer, transaction id, wallet, risk. A later \"suspected forgery\" verdict marks the row. Repeated deliveries (the phone retries until it gets a 2xx) are found by delivery_id and not logged twice.\n\n### Setup\n1. In **Settings**, replace the placeholder with the connection key the phone shows after you add the wallet (paste it only here).\n2. Create a Google Sheet with a header row: received_at, amount, currency, payer_number, payer_name, provider_txn_id, wallet, risk, auto_confirm_ok, transfer_id, delivery_id, status. Select it and your Google credential in the three Google Sheets nodes.\n3. Activate the workflow and copy the Webhook node's **Production URL** into the Qersh app (More, Wallets, Add wallet, \"your store URL\"). \"Test connection\" on the phone must say the signature was verified. Self-hosted n8n needs `NODE_FUNCTION_ALLOW_BUILTIN=crypto` for the Code node; n8n Cloud allows it.\n\n### Customization tips\nAdd columns to the append node as you like (balance_after, payer handle). Keep \"Send sender details\" on \"full name and number\" in the wallet, or the payer number arrives masked. The phone retries a failed delivery for days, so a Sheets outage loses nothing.\n\nQersh (Qersh Pay) is a wallet notification relay, not a payment service provider. Docs: https://qersh.cfd/en/integrations/n8n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
